  "evidence": "Public BeginLogin and LoginSession methods through retained caller-owned RoundTrippers and an owned loopback TLS OAuth server. The default owned pool is created by the actual public constructor, not a private state/constructor seam. Global default-client/transport and entropy overrides run only in isolated child test processes. Exact fixture bytes are compared without normalizing source outcomes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Existing login_migration_contract_test.go and login_contract.rs remain the PKCE, callback, OAuth response, redaction and broad concurrency contracts. This additive fixture uses their synthetic success response and representative callback inputs without copying their entire matrices.",
    "Go-only nil/zero handles, client/state pointer identity, concrete transport assertion and crypto/rand.Reader behavior have explicit go_only names. Rust API shape or pointer/nil equivalence is not assumed.",
    "Exact caller context identity is observed with an injected HTTP client whose Timeout is zero. Values, fixed deadlines, diagnostic scope and actual Done/Err cancellation flow through the real OAuth adapter. Other HTTP-client timeout/redirect/deadline composition is outside this slice.",
    "Injected transports may return OAuth success despite an already canceled/expired caller context. A Rust unconditional context precheck or cancellation race would change this observed contract.",
    "Official Go 1.27.1 crypto/rand.Read terminates the process if an overridden Reader fails. Both entropy stages are observed in isolated fatal children; BeginLogin's recoverable random-error branches remain source-only and are not represented as successful runtime coverage.",
    "The owned default pool uses three separate public sessions and completed HTTP/1.1 TLS exchanges to prove retained routing, independent pools, copied-handle idle release, pre-completion/repeated cleanup and survival of an active response. It establishes no HTTP/2 multiplexing, unfinished HEAD/upload or external-site behavior.",
    "Only synthetic OAuth data and owned local server/test certificate roots are used. No live account, credentials extraction, OS trust/security/native association change, Rust production change, Cargo execution or non-Linux native validation is performed."
  ],
